course: dictionary
lesson: 11234
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Worker» is one of them. Its first meaning is a person who does a job, like a farm worker or an office worker. The words around it tell you which meaning is in use.
explain: «The coloured paint marks that workers spray on the pavement before roadworks are a map.» Here workers are people doing a job, because they spray paint on the road. Ask yourself: who is doing the job, and what are they doing?
explain: Sometimes worker describes how someone works. «A hard worker» puts in lots of effort, and «a fast worker» gets things done quickly. In «worker bees», the word means the bees that do the jobs of the hive.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Foster carers are checked and trained, and social workers visit to make sure children are safe.» Social workers are people whose job is to visit and check on families, so the meaning fits.
fact: A worker is a person who does a job, often to make or build something.
fact: «A hard worker» means someone who works with lots of effort.
fact: «Worker bees» are the bees in a hive that do its jobs, such as collecting nectar.
fact: Words like «office worker», «factory worker» and «aid worker» name the kind of job or place where someone works.
fact: In maths, more workers can often finish a job in less time, if they all work at the same rate.
exercise: What do «worker bees» do in a hive? | *Collect nectar and do the jobs of the hive | Lay all the eggs in the hive | Sleep all winter in the queen's room
exercise: «Foster carers are checked and trained, and social workers visit to make sure children are safe.» Who are social workers? | Children who are very safe | Bees that make honey | *People whose job is to visit and check on children
exercise: Jade says a «hard worker» is someone who is always sleepy. What does hard worker mean? | *Someone who works with lots of effort | Someone who is always tired | Someone who works only at night
test: In the phrase «an office worker», what does worker name? | *A person who does a job in an office | A kind of desk | A type of holiday | A computer game
test: In maths, if more workers are put on a job, what usually happens? | The job stops | The workers get smaller | *The job gets finished in less time | The job takes longer
exam: Which sentence uses worker to mean a bee that does jobs for the hive? | *«The worker bees fly out each morning to collect nectar.» | «The aid worker drove the van across the desert.» | «The hard worker stayed late to finish the report.»
